      "text": "CDC developed the wastewater viral activity level (WVAL) metric to create a standardized method for comparing wastewater data within and across sites. This metric compares current levels to low levels of a virus at a site over the last 24 months.\n\nCDC has validated the WVAL methodology for the following common respiratory illnesses: Influenza A, COVID-19, and RSV."
