  "results": [
    {
      "chunk_id": "oad_readme#0",
      "doc_id": "oad_readme",
      "heading": "ObsAwareData README",
      "text": "Weekly COVID-19, influenza, and RSV surveillance data for all 50 states and the District of Columbia, harmonized from three CDC surveillance systems plus US Census context. It is built for forecasting and nowcasting research, so every value carries a **reliability flag** (`observation_state`) and a pointer back to the exact public source release it came from."
    },
    {
      "chunk_id": "oad_readme#3",
      "doc_id": "oad_readme",
      "heading": "ObsAwareData README > What makes this dataset different",
      "text": "- **Reliability flags on every value.** Each value is labeled `observed_valid`, `observed_zero`, `observed_low_coverage`, `flagged_anomalous`, `incidental_missing`, or `structural_absent`, so a missing or questionable week is never silently treated as a real zero or a normal reading.\n- **Traceable to the source release.** Each row in the long tables records a CDC release that published it (`source_snapshot_id`, `as_of_date`; in the latest-value files, the release that first published its current value); [`metadata/source_snapshots.csv`](metadata/source_snapshots.csv) gives each release's SHA-256 and a link to an unmodified copy of the raw file."
    },
    {
      "chunk_id": "oad_data_dictionary#13",
      "doc_id": "oad_data_dictionary",
      "heading": "ObsAwareData data dictionary > 3. Single-source wide tables",
      "text": "`<st>_nhsn_wide.csv`, `<st>_nssp_wide.csv`, and `<st>_nwss_wide.csv` each start with six key columns:\n\n`analysis_region`, `analysis_region_type`, `analysis_region_id`, `raw_geography_type`, `raw_geography_id`, `observation_week`\n\nThese are followed by a pair of columns for every measure and pathogen the source publishes:\n\n| Column name | Holds |\n|---|---|\n| `<measure>_<pathogen>` | the value (`weekly_feature` in the long table) |\n| `<measure>_<pathogen>_flag` | its reliability flag (`observation_state` in the long table) |"
