      "chunk_id": "nhsn_hrd_qa#33",
      "doc_id": "nhsn_hrd_qa",
      "heading": "HRD Data Processing and Quality Assurance Reference Guide",
      "text": "May 2025\n\n10\no Note: A facility status of \u2018A\u2019 indicates that the hospital currently has an Active registration\nwith NHSN\nAfter exclusion criteria are applied, the weekly hospital data are then aggregated to various geographic\nlevels (nation, HHS region, state/territory) allowing for calculation of aggregate metrics, including hospital\nadmission rates and inpatient and ICU occupancy percentages. These aggregate data are published to\ndata.cdc.gov and CDC\u2019s NHSN HRD website every Friday afternoon.\nAdditional Resources\n\u2022 CDC\u2019S NHSN Hospital Respiratory Data\n\u2022 Hospital Respiratory Data Weekly Reporting Form\n\u2022 Hospital Respiratory Data Table of Instructions\n\u2022 Hospital Respiratory Data Daily Reporting Form\n\u2022 Hospital Respiratory Data Table of Instructions"
    },
    {
      "chunk_id": "oad_data_sources#3",
      "doc_id": "oad_data_sources",
      "heading": "ObsAwareData data sources > 1. Hospital admissions: NHSN Hospital Respiratory Data (HRD)",
      "text": "- **Fields used:** total new admissions with a confirmed diagnosis (COVID-19, influenza, RSV), and the number of hospitals reporting those admissions. All other HRD fields are excluded: bed occupancy, ICU counts, age breakdowns, rates, and change measures.\n- **Geography:** State (jurisdiction). DC is included; territories and national or regional aggregates are excluded.\n- **Note:** Hospitals were not required to report RSV admissions before August 2024. RSV hospital data for weeks up to 2024-08-03 are therefore marked `structural_absent`, not missing."
    },
    {
      "chunk_id": "oad_methods#14",
      "doc_id": "oad_methods",
      "heading": "ObsAwareData methods > 4. How the thresholds were set",
      "text": "| Rule | South Carolina tail share |\n   |---|---|\n   | NHSN reporting-hospital count | 10.1% of pathogen-weeks |\n   | NHSN admission change | 6.14% of pathogen-weeks |\n   | NSSP smoothed change | 10.75% of region-pathogen-weeks |\n   | NWSS coverage ratio | 22.6% (COVID-19), 21.4% (influenza), 19.2% (RSV) of site-pathogen pairs |\n\nEach state's threshold is the value that cuts off that share of its own distribution, computed from the latest release. Applying the method to South Carolina itself gives values close to its fixed ones for hospital admissions and ED visits: 58 vs. 50 hospitals, 99% vs. 100%, and 35%.\n\n**Wastewater.** The wastewater target shares (22.6%, 21.4%, 19.2%) are the shares originally intended for South Carolina. South Carolina's own wastewater cutoffs are derived with the same percentile method as every other state, which gives 0.75, 0.76, and 0.76."
    },
    {
      "chunk_id": "resp_faq#10",
      "doc_id": "resp_faq",
      "heading": "Release Notes and Frequently Asked Questions (Respiratory Illnesses Data Channel) > Understanding the data > Hospital Admissions Level",
      "text": "- Metrics and inclusion criteria: Many hospital subtypes, including acute care and critical access hospitals, are included in the calculations for determining the hospital admissions levels. Psychiatric, rehabilitation, and religious non-medical hospital types are excluded from calculations. Hospitals that reported complete admissions data to NHSN during a given week are included in the calculations and the visualization.\n\n- Data quality and timeliness: While CDC reviews reported data for completeness and errors and corrects those found, some reporting errors might still exist within the data. CDC and partners work with reporting sites to correct any errors and update the data in subsequent weeks. Data for the most recent two weeks may be affected by potential reporting delays; caution should be taken when interpreting these data.\n\n- The hospital admissions levels are determined based on the respiratory virus-associated hospitalization rates, which are calculated as the total number of new hospital admissions reported to NHSN for a given reporting week (Sunday \u2013 Saturday) divided by the total population (per 100,000) as per the U.S. Census vintage 2023 population estimates."
    },
    {
      "chunk_id": "oad_data_dictionary#18",
      "doc_id": "oad_data_dictionary",
      "heading": "ObsAwareData data dictionary > 5. Measures",
      "text": "| `feature_name` | Source | Pathogens | Unit | `definition_status` | Meaning |\n|---|---|---|---|---|---|\n| `hospital_admission_count` | NHSN | covid, influenza, rsv | `count` | confirmed | New hospital admissions in the week with a laboratory-confirmed diagnosis, all ages. |\n| `hospital_reporting_count` | NHSN | covid, influenza, rsv | `count` | confirmed | Number of hospitals that reported that week for that pathogen: the denominator behind the admission count. |\n| `coverage_status` | NHSN (derived) | covid, influenza, rsv | `categorical_coverage_status` | uncertain | `full_participation` or `reduced_participation` (fewer reporting hospitals than the state's threshold; see [METHODS.md](METHODS.md)). Blank when `structural_absent`. |"
    }
  ]
}

